cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use arbital, please cite it as below."
title: "arbital: Association Radii By Information-Theoretic Association Learning"
abstract: >-
  A visual method and Python package for exploring general association
  between variables. For a chosen target, each other variable is measured
  with both a correlation-based statistic and mutual information and drawn
  as an orbit around the target, so that non-monotone dependence invisible
  to correlation becomes visible.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Byrne
    given-names: Aaron
    email: aaron@aaronbyrnephd.com
version: 0.1.1
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/aaronbyrnephd/arbital"
keywords:
  - association
  - mutual information
  - feature selection
  - exploratory data analysis
  - data visualization
